{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513166-so-if-you-pick-humanistic-tenets","id":1513166,"title":"So if you pick Humanistic tenets...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-28T23:42:42-07:00","id":1513166,"title":"So if you pick Humanistic tenets...","content":"Is it even possible to own ghouls? Because you are renewing their slavery every time you feed them. So that's, BLAM, three stains every month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T03:02:48-07:00","id":1513180,"title":"","content":"Sure, just get used to the fact that your humanity is going to be mid-tier at best.<br /> <br /> You can also theoretically mitigate it by having convictions that mitigate the stains (for example, if tenets and/or convictions believe that all killing is bad and life is sacred and blah; saving a person's life by ghouling them; ghouling a violent criminal to keep them under control without killing them, etc)<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T13:21:13-07:00","id":1513225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513166-so-if-you-pick-humanistic-tenets#post1513166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it even possible to own ghouls? Because you are renewing their slavery every time you feed them. So that's, BLAM, three stains every month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they would see ghouls as disposable slaves and see it as more proof of how far you have fallen and how you have to justify your actions of having them around. Even my Malkavian who is a somewhat caring dude is totally self aware of the hyprocrisy of needing them and while he will reward good work when he can. He does know that he is harming them in the long run and it does bother him from time to time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-30-2023, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T16:31:34-07:00","id":1522650,"title":"","content":"Well, as an old Sabbath fan, I avoid tenets that are too prim and proper. I'll be stained anyways, my tenets don't need to be a source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T10:55:30-07:00","id":1522713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513166-so-if-you-pick-humanistic-tenets#post1513166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it even possible to own ghouls? Because you are renewing their slavery every time you feed them. So that's, BLAM, three stains every month.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's going to be somewhat dependent on how you do things. You can ghoul a mortal without blood bonding them by not having them drink from the vein. Ghouling isn't in and of itself a stain, but bonding is (V5 core pg. 240). And ghouls aren't slaves unless you blood bond them; you could have a positive relationship with the ghoul without the staining. It'd be somewhat hard to keep up with, but you could do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T12:15:50-07:00","id":1522718,"title":"","content":"I would argue that you are enslaving them with supernatural powers and agelessness and to keep that perk is that you better play ball especially if you have lived past a natural lifespan. That no matter how you cut it is that being a ghoul is a life of slavery serving inhuman things. The blood bond doesn\u2019t need to be a factor after a period of time as they realized they made a Faustian deal to gain some sort of advantage and even having a good relationship with them doesn\u2019t the fact that you have slaves to help you manage your daily affairs as you slumber.<br /> <br /> This reminds me of my How you treat your ghouls post I did sometime ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-17-2023, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T23:39:21-07:00","id":1522734,"title":"","content":"I think this is comes down to the perspective <br /> If you not bound them - tho even that could be worked around with clever RP - you not really enslaving them<br /> Just always give them the option to chose<br /> They will always chose you, and not because of blood or some faustian deals... in a Hmanistic tenets oriented game even as a monster your goal is not to be one<br /> The ghouls works for you if you not bound it - and truth to be told, an average Joe spends his meaningless life working to a company in a soulcrushing job witch is way worse<br /> In this case WoD 'atmosphere&quot; eg. Darkness with a capital D works on your favor - but the sad reality is, even IRL our jobs where we toil our life away for minimum wage (or better) is way worse than working to a vampire who' only asks to manage her daily affairs while sleeps<br /> Look deep in to your soul and answer me: wouldn't you chose the vampire and be a part something bigger and have the perks? <br /> Or anyone you know?<br /> Would you regret it?<br /> In the grand scheme of things, you give some extra meaning to the life of that ghoul - sometimes giving them the gift of &quot;immortality&quot; - even a few years of prolonged life - is meaning so much to them, you can't possibly comprehend<br /> When my grandfather asked every year from my grandmother what she wants for her birthday, she always answered &quot;one more year with you&quot;<br /> Of course you don't have to use elders as ghouls but I think you can see my point <br /> <br /> Thats why it is important to chose your ghoul carefully by the way<br /> <br /> Remember, it all started with the Humanistic tenets that were picked, so the &quot;they would see ghouls as disposable slaves and see it as more proof of how far you have fallen and how you have to justify your actions of having them around.&quot; not really a factor, because... you wont. Thats the whole point. <br /> You simply wont<br /> Ideally you talked through the chosen Tenets in your group, so that all players understand what they mean and what kind of actions would consist violations of these Tenets<br /> So if they remain true to that, or at least try - and people tend to forget how important the fact, you at leats tried and not gave in to nihilism at the first second - keeping a ghouls wouldn't be an issue<br /> And if not? Well you not really cared about those stains anway in the first place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T23:55:40-07:00","id":1522735,"title":"","content":"I'd say that it's not just a factor of how you treat your ghouls. The horror of ghouldom is in the very nature of this condition. <br /> <br /> You are purposefully throwing someone into an addiction from which at a certain point only death would be a release. <br /> <br /> Ghouls are obsessed by their domitors, so you are also damaging their mental stability, their families, friendships and relations. <br /> <br /> Treating ghouls fairly may condone some, but under a Humanistic set of tenets I feel ghouls should rightly be a cause for Stains. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T10:44:33-07:00","id":1522751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513166-so-if-you-pick-humanistic-tenets?p=1522735#post1522735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that it's not just a factor of how you treat your ghouls. The horror of ghouldom is in the very nature of this condition.<br /> <br /> You are purposefully throwing someone into an addiction from which at a certain point only death would be a release.<br /> <br /> Ghouls are obsessed by their domitors, so you are also damaging their mental stability, their families, friendships and relations.<br /> <br /> Treating ghouls fairly may condone some, but under a Humanistic set of tenets I feel ghouls should rightly be a cause for Stains.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Like it's been said it's going to make your humanity wane to mid tier levels of 5 or 6 at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}